// idiom: effect-acquire
// summary: the acquisition of an `effect ... undo ...`: the value the component holds while it is active
// rule: G4: every acquisition carries its inverse in the same statement, `undo <inverse>`
// rule: G7: teardown runs the inverses in reverse order of acquisition, so nothing is released by hand
// fill: Map.new()
// type: Map[Str, Int]

component Counter {
  let store = effect Map.new() undo store.drop()
}
